---- Wrap-up pass 2 (2026-09-07) ----

[F-7] create_file / edit_file failing repeatedly on big files — root cause in the SSE parsers: (a) a final `data:` line without a trailing newline was never processed, so a gateway closing the stream right after the last delta lost the closing bytes of the tool arguments; (b) per-chunk lossy UTF-8 decode could mangle multi-byte chars split across chunks; (c) unparseable lines were dropped silently. All four adapters (OpenAI chat/responses, Claude, Gemini) now use a byte-level `SseLineBuffer` with EOF flush + debug logging of dropped lines. Tool descriptions also tell the model to keep a single call under ~6K chars and append in chunks.
[R-2] tauri_plugin_updater filtered to `error` in the default log filter (offline check no longer WARNs; the startup check is already silent in the UI).
[R-3] "Provider is slow to respond — no data for Ns" notice after 30s of stream silence (StreamSlow event, both hosts, rendered by the stream banner; clears on the next delta). 180s hard abort unchanged.
[R-4] Alphabetical is the default project order; once the user drag-reorders, that order wins everywhere (Explorer, Search, SCM, Agent all read the same list) and persists. "Sort A→Z" button in the Explorer header resets it.
[R-5] Added the `image` crate (MIT/Apache-2.0, decoders only). Images >8000px on a side or >5MB are downscaled / re-encoded at ingestion (`media_store::normalize_for_providers`); auto-stub+retry remains as fallback.
[R-6] Search scope on panel open = both context projects (file's project first, then chat's) — verified in code; "only the top project" was the pre-fix default.

---- UI / UX (reported by user) ----

[F-1] Project list in the left panel is sorted alphabetically (explorer store, load + add).

[F-2] Chat created before opening the agent panel was invisible until reload — `ensureTask` appended the new task past the tree's 5-item history cap; now prepended and the project node auto-expands.

[F-3] Git operations (checkout / create branch / commit / push / pull / fetch / sync / undo / discard-all) show a per-project busy label + spinner in the SCM header.

[F-4] "Quoted" command output while the agent runs — the PTY echo stripper only matched single-line echoes; long commands wrap across ConPTY prompt repaints and leaked. Now matches head/tail fragments so the model only sees real output.

[F-5] OpenAI 400 "Unsupported parameter: 'max_tokens' … use 'max_completion_tokens'" (new models breaking) — per-model request parameters are configurable in Register/Edit model → "Request parameters (advanced)": max-tokens key, temperature, top_p, reasoning effort, thinking budget, parallel_tool_calls, tool_choice, stop (Auto / Send / Omit), omit list, extra body JSON. On a 400 "Unsupported parameter: X" the executor retries without X and persists the override for that model automatically (both hosts).

[F-6] Explorer / Search / Source Control auto-reveal the current project when opened: the active editor file's project first, then the active chat's project; both expanded, first scrolled into view, nothing else collapsed. Search scopes to those projects.

